{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "01302",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 0.67,
      "end_seconds": 4.8,
      "duration_seconds": 4.13,
      "text": "Oh, morning, doctor. Lovely to meet you."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 5.53,
      "end_seconds": 9.97,
      "duration_seconds": 4.44,
      "text": "Of course leave it there. How can I help?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 10.68,
      "end_seconds": 16.4,
      "duration_seconds": 5.72,
      "text": "hello doctor. I'm here with them in case I can help"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 17.49,
      "end_seconds": 20.79,
      "duration_seconds": 3.3,
      "text": "Alright please do. Extra information is always welcome."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 21.94,
      "end_seconds": 32.65,
      "duration_seconds": 10.71,
      "text": "Let me think, it's burning when I pass urine. I thought I'd wait, but it hasn't gone."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 34.03,
      "end_seconds": 36.87,
      "duration_seconds": 2.84,
      "text": "Okay, did it come on recently?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 38.89,
      "end_seconds": 41.75,
      "duration_seconds": 2.86,
      "text": "About... well about two weeks."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 43.85,
      "end_seconds": 52.32,
      "duration_seconds": 8.47,
      "text": "Tell me a bit more about it: how bad it gets, how often, and whether anything makes it better or worse."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 53.81,
      "end_seconds": 62.05,
      "duration_seconds": 8.24,
      "text": "hmm, it settles a little with drinking water. I'd say all the time"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 63.27,
      "end_seconds": 65.66,
      "duration_seconds": 2.39,
      "text": "is there anything else with it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 70.77,
      "end_seconds": 114.64,
      "duration_seconds": 43.87,
      "text": "it it usually comes with cloudy urine. Uh, I've been needing to go all the time too, since last night. As for needing to go all the time, mild, really. Sorry, what was I saying, as for cloudy urine, I honestly can't say when that began. It might have been last month or the month before. A dull ache above the pubic bone was there, but it's gone away on its own"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 115.26,
      "end_seconds": 119.7,
      "duration_seconds": 4.44,
      "text": "have you noticed new partner vomiting or blood in the urine?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 121.51,
      "end_seconds": 128.84,
      "duration_seconds": 7.33,
      "text": "Let me think uh no no new partner vomiting or blood in the urine."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 129.93,
      "end_seconds": 133.82,
      "duration_seconds": 3.89,
      "text": "A few quick ones: fever or vaginal discharge?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 134.61,
      "end_seconds": 140.16,
      "duration_seconds": 5.55,
      "text": "Ah, um, no, no fever or vaginal discharge."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 141.44,
      "end_seconds": 144.24,
      "duration_seconds": 2.8,
      "text": "any muscle or joint problems besides this?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 148.41,
      "end_seconds": 151.1,
      "duration_seconds": 2.69,
      "text": "No, uh, nothing there."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 152.9,
      "end_seconds": 157.25,
      "duration_seconds": 4.35,
      "text": "tell me about any past illnesses or ongoing conditions"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 159.35,
      "end_seconds": 169.09,
      "duration_seconds": 9.74,
      "text": "ah, I've had diabetes for five years now ah, I have high blood pressure, for about ten years"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 169.9,
      "end_seconds": 179.66,
      "duration_seconds": 9.76,
      "text": "hm, okay alright, diabetes and high blood pressure, that matches what I have here what about your parents, brothers or sisters, any conditions?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 180.69,
      "end_seconds": 187.59,
      "duration_seconds": 6.9,
      "text": "Mm, my grandmother had dementia. I mean, um, my cousin has psoriasis."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 202.74,
      "end_seconds": 205.56,
      "duration_seconds": 2.82,
      "text": "anything you do to stay fit?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 206.94,
      "end_seconds": 210.64,
      "duration_seconds": 3.7,
      "text": "I do a yoga class on Thursdays."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 211.91,
      "end_seconds": 214.0,
      "duration_seconds": 2.09,
      "text": "So, who lives with you?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 215.78,
      "end_seconds": 218.35,
      "duration_seconds": 2.57,
      "text": "My partner and our baby."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 231.91,
      "end_seconds": 236.77,
      "duration_seconds": 4.86,
      "text": "are you allergic to anything? Any allergies to medicines or foods?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 237.98,
      "end_seconds": 241.23,
      "duration_seconds": 3.25,
      "text": "No I'm not allergic to anything."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 254.72,
      "end_seconds": 258.88,
      "duration_seconds": 4.16,
      "text": "can you list what you take, tablets, creams or inhalers?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 260.28,
      "end_seconds": 265.66,
      "duration_seconds": 5.38,
      "text": "it's glibenclamide 5 milligrams maybe before breakfast for my sugar"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 267.23,
      "end_seconds": 272.04,
      "duration_seconds": 4.81,
      "text": "Do you have the packet or the prescription with you?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 273.03,
      "end_seconds": 282.19,
      "duration_seconds": 9.16,
      "text": "let me think, you know, no, it's at home it's lisinopril, 10 milligrams, once a day"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 283.48,
      "end_seconds": 286.0,
      "duration_seconds": 2.52,
      "text": "how long have you taken that?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 287.77,
      "end_seconds": 292.14,
      "duration_seconds": 4.37,
      "text": "About six months. It's cranberry juice, every day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 292.7,
      "end_seconds": 296.21,
      "duration_seconds": 3.51,
      "text": "time for your numbers, if that's okay"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 304.01,
      "end_seconds": 306.81,
      "duration_seconds": 2.8,
      "text": "bear with me while this finishes.."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 325.59,
      "end_seconds": 333.82,
      "duration_seconds": 8.23,
      "text": "Okay: temperature is 36.6 degrees, saturation 97 percent, BP is 126 over 72. And pulse 64."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 336.56,
      "end_seconds": 341.33,
      "duration_seconds": 4.77,
      "text": "I'll need to examine you for this, it won't take long."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 342.16,
      "end_seconds": 344.62,
      "duration_seconds": 2.46,
      "text": "take a deep breath for me"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 355.51,
      "end_seconds": 361.99,
      "duration_seconds": 6.48,
      "text": "Your tummy is soft with mild tenderness low down and no pain in the loins."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 364.82,
      "end_seconds": 376.29,
      "duration_seconds": 11.47,
      "text": "thank you you can get dressed from what you've told me and what I found my working impression is a lower urinary tract infection. Vaginal irritation is still possible"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 377.6,
      "end_seconds": 379.71,
      "duration_seconds": 2.11,
      "text": "Will it clear up?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 380.8,
      "end_seconds": 413.83,
      "duration_seconds": 33.03,
      "text": "it's reasonable to be concerned, but right now a lower urinary tract infection is my leading thought, not anything worse. We should do a urine culture for recurrent urinary infection. I'd rather check than guess, and this is the quickest way to to know more. I'll request a urine test, it'll help with dysuria. That will help us see what's going on underneath and decide the next step"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 415.31,
      "end_seconds": 447.09,
      "duration_seconds": 31.78,
      "text": "You'll be taking nitrofurantoin 100 milligrams twice a day for three days. You take it by mouth. That's for urinary infection. Drink plenty of water and don't hold on when you need to go. And please bring the latest prescription or the medicine boxes to the next visit so we can settle the dose. The thing that would worry me is if you get fever loin pain or vomiting. If that happens go to emergency."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0044",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 452.26,
      "end_seconds": 453.8,
      "duration_seconds": 1.54,
      "text": "I'll remember that"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0045",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 455.87,
      "end_seconds": 459.5,
      "duration_seconds": 3.63,
      "text": "I'll want another look after the culture result."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0046",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 460.08,
      "end_seconds": 463.5,
      "duration_seconds": 3.42,
      "text": "uh, I can manage that"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0047",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 465.02,
      "end_seconds": 469.12,
      "duration_seconds": 4.1,
      "text": "That's everything on my side. Anything you're unsure about?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0048",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 470.71,
      "end_seconds": 474.15,
      "duration_seconds": 3.44,
      "text": "Hmm, alright, thanks, take care."
    }
  ]
}